Upstream attribution
====================

chiaki-ng
Repository: https://github.com/chiaki-ng/chiaki-ng
Pinned baseline: c8bea2642d0e95402f373af55584a3b98cd89417
License: LicenseRef-AGPL-3.0-only-OpenSSL

The GPSx SRCH discovery formatter and response parser are behavioral Rust ports
from `lib/include/chiaki/discovery.h`, `lib/src/discovery.c`,
`lib/include/chiaki/http.h`, and `lib/src/http.c` at the pinned baseline.

The GPSx registration-only cryptographic behavior is a Rust port from
`lib/include/chiaki/rpcrypt.h`, `lib/src/rpcrypt.c`, and `test/rpcrypt.c` at
the pinned baseline. It is confined to the PS4/PS5 registration key schedule,
aeropause transformation, fixed-counter HMAC-SHA-256 IV, and AES-128-CFB.

Third-party Rust cryptography dependencies
===========================================

The `gpsx-crypto` crate uses the following crates from the RustCrypto project
under MIT OR Apache-2.0: aead 0.5.2, aes 0.8.4, aes-gcm 0.10.3, cfb-mode
0.8.2, ctr 0.9.2, ghash 0.5.1, hmac 0.12.1, opaque-debug 0.3.1, polyval
0.6.2, sha2 0.10.9, universal-hash 0.5.1, cipher 0.4.4, crypto-common
0.1.7, digest 0.10.7, inout 0.1.4, and block-buffer 0.10.4. It also uses
rand_core 0.6.4 and zeroize 1.9.1 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT),
subtle 2.6.1 (BSD-3-Clause), cfg-if 1.0.5 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), cpufeatures
0.2.17 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), generic-array 0.14.7 (MIT), typenum 1.20.1
(MIT OR Apache-2.0), version_check 0.9.5 (MIT/Apache-2.0), and libc 0.2.191
(MIT OR Apache-2.0). Their license texts and notices remain those distributed
by their respective packages.

